{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1454595-psiads-vs-psions","id":1454595,"title":"Psiads vs Psions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-09T12:21:44-07:00","id":1454595,"title":"Psiads vs Psions","content":"I don't have the source books and only know a few things about them like how psions are technically stronger but psiads are way more flexible. But when put against each how do they stack up when compared. Like what can psions do that psiads can't and the other way round what are psiads capable of that psions can't do.<br /> <br /> I know psiads are limited in high levels for modes (I think this is right) and psions can only learn certain modes I think<br /> <br /> Psiads can combine modes and psions can't <br /> <br /> But what I want to know is what does this mean in a game.<br /> <br /> From what I've been told around the forums I would prefer to be psiad and lean pretty heavily in this direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T12:47:00-07:00","id":1454597,"title":"","content":"You'll eventually be able to do a little bit of everything as a Psiad, but will be handily outperformed in any single area by a Psion. <br /> <br /> Great flexibility, low power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T13:22:01-07:00","id":1454602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeonstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1454595-psiads-vs-psions#post1454595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the source books and only know a few things about them like how psions are technically stronger but psiads are way more flexible. But when put against each how do they stack up when compared. Like what can psions do that psiads can't and the other way round what are psiads capable of that psions can't do.<br /> <br /> I know psiads are limited in high levels for modes (I think this is right) and psions can only learn certain modes I think<br /> <br /> Psiads can combine modes and psions can't<br /> <br /> But what I want to know is what does this mean in a game.<br /> <br /> From what I've been told around the forums I would prefer to be psiad and lean pretty heavily in this direction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mostly got it, I\u2019m not sure what else you\u2019re asking. Psions have one Aptitude that they can learn all three modes of up to the 5th dot, and can only learn the first dot of any other Modes (these ceilings both rise at the Proxy level, but we\u2019ll keep this simple at the normal PC level). They can also use their Aptitude to enhance other Psions in thematic ways (Clairvoyance increasing range, teleportation enhancing area of effect, etc etc).<br /> <br /> Psiads favor 2 Aptitudes as a Psi 2 starting character and can learn all six of the Modes up to the third dot, and gain the first dot in other Modes. At Psi 3 they can gain the second dots in those other modes. At Psi 5 they can gain 3 dots in any Mode. There is an edge that lets them buy ONE favored Mode up to the 4th dot. Again leaving out Proxy level discussion for now. Psiads do not have the versatility to enhance other Psi users that Psions have, they\u2019re only able to enhance the effective Psi rating of someone who shares a favored Aptitude with them by one, and be so enhanced in turn. PSIONS are artificially designed to be highly specialized teamwork weapons, while Psiads are evolved to be more self sufficient jack of all trades, masters of none.<br /> <br /> Note that no Psiad favors Teleportation or Quantakinesis as Psi 2, but they all gain Quantakinesis as a third favored Aptitude at Psi 3.<br /> <br /> Any Psi user can try to combine their modes to create creative effects, but obviously Psiads have an advantage here being able to learn a greater variety of Modes. Psions are more likely to combine Modes with a partner. The exact rules on these creative effects I believe are getting fleshed out in the forthcoming book Prometheus Unbound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-10-2021, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T13:25:47-07:00","id":1454603,"title":"","content":"Is psi 5 the max a psiad can teach or is there a way to get higher and if so what effect does it have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T13:42:33-07:00","id":1454608,"title":"","content":"They can get to proxy tier, but they can't use the 5th dot of their primary aptitudes without an edge, and they can't use the 6th or 7th dot powers at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T14:43:48-07:00","id":1454611,"title":"","content":"Another big difference between the two is in character creation and character advancement.<br /> <br /> A psion gets 4 dots of powers, and can put all 4 dots in the same Mode (generating psionic dysfunction, but giving them an impressive bonus to that Mode), while a psiad only gets 3 dots and can't put more than 2 dots in a Mode. They also start with one fewer dots worth of Psi or Attributes.<br /> <br /> As they go up in level, psiads get fewer psi points and worse attunement range, max out their Psi score (and everything based on that Psi score) at a lower level, and pay more xp to increase their Psi and Modes. Their psionic Edges also tend to cost more.<br /> <br /> Over the course of their careers a psion can learn a maximum of 61 psi powers ([21 Modes x 2 dots] + [3 Modes x 6 dots] + 1 seveth level power) while a psiad can learn up to 82 ([15 Modes x 3 dots] + [9 Modes x 4 dots] + 1 mode with a bonus dot), but the difference in xp costs and the lower max level of the psiad powers skews this result when comparing their power potential.<br /> <br /> I think psiads work a lot better in a game with Talents than in a mixed group with psions unless you let the psiad use the psion character creation rules and adapt the psion xp chart, with Aptitude=Primary Aptitude and Auxiliary Mode=Secondary Aptitude. That lets the psiad leverage their breadth of power versus a psion's depth of power without getting completely marginalized due to winding up with fewer actual powers because of the differing xp costs. Otherwise, it is hard to claim a psiad has greater versatility when all their psion comrades have more powers (and of a higher level) than they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 07-09-2021, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T20:24:10-07:00","id":1454635,"title":"","content":"I agree with Shepherdboi. in our games, Psiads suffer badly from the xp issue, especially if they're in a game with more than a few psions, mainly because you need to be <i>really</i> flexcible to make up for largely missing out of four dot and above powers, which is where the real OH COME ON! powers hang out. <br /> <br /> that being said, they work <i>really </i>well as a rare character type in the base Aeon games, where their powers really7 let them shine with talents, and the lack of the higher level powers doesn't really create an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T00:56:41-07:00","id":1454646,"title":"","content":"Psiads starting with fewer dots in Modes and Attributes is a thematic reflection of the difference in their nature vs the artificially enhanced Psions, but nothing breaks if you want to create more parity leveling out those differences in starting scores (note: things would become unbalanced in Psiads\u2019 favor if you lifted the cap on Mode Scores, as that\u2019s the primary advantage Psions have making up for their limitation to one favored Aptitude).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T16:29:54-07:00","id":1454663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1454595-psiads-vs-psions?p=1454646#post1454646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psiads starting with fewer dots in Modes and Attributes is a thematic reflection of the difference in their nature vs the artificially enhanced Psions</div> </div> </div> </div>It seemed odd to me that they felt the need to start psiads off with fewer power dots since, even though psions are genetically turbo-charged to be super effective, starting character psions are generally assumed to gain their four dots over their first few weeks out of a Prometheus chamber, while psiads seem to be assumed to take years to gain their three dots, yet progress only slightly slower than psions in play.<br /> <br /> This interpretation is supported by the fact that the only psiad specific Path is an <i>Origin</i> path, which would apply to their formative years as children/adolescents. <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u00c6on \u00c6xpansion</span></span> indicates most psiads develop powers between their mid-teens and late twenties, suggesting many starting psiads have had their powers for five to ten years before play began, yet are still only Psi 2 with 3 dots of powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T21:02:01-07:00","id":1454671,"title":"","content":"Psiads can pull off combined effects a lot easier and technically cheaper. They have less Psi points in total though which...is an issue that I haven't seen mentioned yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T21:25:38-07:00","id":1454672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1454595-psiads-vs-psions?p=1454671#post1454671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psiads can pull off combined effects a lot easier and technically cheaper. They have less Psi points in total though which...is an issue that I haven't seen mentioned yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the lack of higher level powers means they usually don't need as many Psi points. Most of their powers are either free or need just 1 point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T22:14:06-07:00","id":1454673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1454595-psiads-vs-psions?p=1454672#post1454672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the lack of higher level powers means they usually don't need as many Psi points. Most of their powers are either free or need just 1 point.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but a lot of their flexibility is predicated on activating multiple abilities simultaneously to combine effects. Plus it never feels good to move down a step.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}